# kensaiapp instance environment — TEMPLATE
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (untracked) and adjust for your machine:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored, so machine-specific values never enter the tracked/public repo.

# CORE — the root the skills/loaders resolve `<CORE>` to (doctrine, flow + cross-role
# contracts, engineering + setup templates). A SessionStart hook reads this value.
#
# Default (ready-to-run): the vendored core inside this repo. Leave as-is unless you
# have centralized core to a shared location (see `kensaiapp-set-core`), in which case
# point this at that absolute path.
CORE=core/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-local paths the launchers read — from the ENVIRONMENT, not from this file.
#
# Nothing reads these two out of `.env`: the launchers are shell scripts that read
# only the environment they are started in, and so does the hook that notifies on
# a subagent's stop. Export them where your shell sets its environment, such as
# your shell's profile; the commented lines below show the value, not where it goes.
#
# Both are OPTIONAL and both are deliberately undefaulted. A shared tool under
# `core/` must not bake in a host path (kensaiapp_structure.md § core/tools), so
# each launcher takes these from the environment and says plainly what it is
# skipping when one is unset — rather than guessing at a location on your disk.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# NOTIFIER — an executable taking one message argument, called when a background
# run finishes. Every launcher detaches `watch_agent.py` against it. Unset means
# runs still launch and still complete; you simply are not told when they do.
# Example:
# export KENSAIAPP_NOTIFIER=/absolute/path/to/notify.sh

# EVAL HISTORY — where `launch-skill-evals` archives each finished round, keyed
# <skill>/evals/workspace/iteration-N. `.claude/skills/*/evals/workspace/` is
# gitignored and a round run in a worktree dies with that worktree, so this copy
# is the only lasting record of what a round measured. Unset means the round
# still runs and still commits its summary, but leaves no out-of-repo archive.
# Example:
# export KENSAIAPP_EVAL_HISTORY=/absolute/path/to/kensaiapp-eval-history
